---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CaseStudy from "../components/CaseStudy.astro";
import CaseHero from "../components/CaseHero.astro";
import Figure from "../components/Figure.astro";
import Intro from "../components/Intro.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import FeatureColumns from "../components/FeatureColumns.astro";
import FeatureBox from "../components/FeatureBox.astro";
import NextProject from "../components/NextProject.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";

import hero from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/hero.png";
import wireframe1 from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/wireframe-1.png";
import wireframe2 from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/wireframe-2.png";
import wireframe3 from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/wireframe-3.png";
import wireframe4 from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/wireframe-4.png";
import prototype from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/prototype.png";
import dark1 from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/dashboard-dark-1.png";
import dark2 from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/dashboard-dark-2.png";
import dashboards from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/dashboards.png";
import dragAndDrop from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/drag-and-drop.png";
import atAGlance from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/at-a-glance.png";
import mobile from "../assets/images/trading-workbench/mobile.png";

const wireframes = [
  { src: wireframe1, alt: "Wireframe: portfolio overview dashboard" },
  { src: wireframe2, alt: "Wireframe: dashboard with widget areas highlighted" },
  { src: wireframe3, alt: "Wireframe: empty dashboard ready for widgets" },
  { src: wireframe4, alt: "Wireframe: market overview" },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Trading Workbench: designing a trading platform for VZ — Fábio Silva"
  description="Case study: designing Trading Workbench, a responsive trading platform with real-time data and customisable dashboards, built at ti&m and delivered to VZ."
>
  <CaseHero
    title="Trading Workbench: a trading platform for beginners and professionals"
    lead="Market information and trading, brought closer to everyday banking. A responsive platform with real-time data and fully customisable dashboards, designed at ti&m and delivered to VZ."
    meta="Senior Interaction Designer · VZ, via ti&m · 2021"
  />

  <CaseStudy>
    <div class="section stack">
      <Figure src={hero} alt="Trading Workbench portfolio overview dashboard" priority />
      <Intro
        items={[
          {
            label: "About",
            text: "Trading Workbench is a responsive trading platform for banks, built at ti&m for beginners and professionals alike. It covers portfolio monitoring, a real-time market overview, detailed instrument views and trade execution, with several markets to browse and watchlists to build. We delivered it to VZ.",
          },
          {
            label: "In brief",
            text: "Bring market information and trading closer to everyday banking, in one platform that works for beginners and professionals.",
          },
          {
            label: "Impact",
            text: "A trading platform delivered to VZ, with real-time data, customisable dashboards and a mobile version for use on the go. Users gave good feedback.",
          },
        ]}
      />
    </div>

    <section class="section stack">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Goals" title="Where it all began.">
        <p>
          The brief was to bring market prices and market information closer to e-banking functions and data, in one
          platform. The client already had an idea of the main features. We took it as a starting point, not a final
          list.
        </p>
      </SectionHeader>
      <FeatureColumns
        items={[
          {
            title: "One place for markets and banking",
            text: "Portfolio, market overview, instrument details and trading together, close to the client’s own banking data.",
          },
          {
            title: "Beginners and professionals",
            text: "A platform that is approachable for newcomers and keeps the depth experienced traders expect.",
          },
          {
            title: "Everything at a glance",
            text: "In the moment of buying or selling, users need the important information in front of them to decide.",
          },
        ]}
      />
    </section>

    <div class="section section--wide">
      <div class="grid-2 wireframes">
        {wireframes.map((w) => <Figure src={w.src} alt={w.alt} maxWidth={530} />)}
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section stack">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Process" title="Challenge the list, then prototype.">
        <p>
          The client came with an idea of the main features, and we challenged it together. We started by analysing the
          core features, then used wireframes to visualise how everything could come together.
        </p>
        <p>
          We took our time through the prototype, test and feedback phases, and only started the high-fidelity design
          once we felt confident in the direction.
        </p>
        <p>
          I designed the dashboard, widgets and instrument view, and ran the prototype tests with internal users and
          potential clients on the VZ side.
        </p>
      </SectionHeader>
      <Figure src={prototype} alt="High-fidelity prototype of the Trading Workbench dashboard" />
    </section>

    <section class="section stack">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Challenge" title="A lot of data, one decision.">
        <p>
          A trading platform has a lot to show at once: real-time prices, charts, news, the client’s portfolio and order
          entry. At the moment of a trade, the user needs the important parts in one glance. Three things had to work
          together:
        </p>
      </SectionHeader>
      <FeatureColumns
        items={[
          { text: "Give professionals the depth they expect without overwhelming beginners." },
          { text: "Bring market data and e-banking information into one platform that feels like one product." },
          { text: "Keep it pleasant enough to use every day." },
        ]}
      />
      <Figure src={dark1} alt="Dark-theme instrument view with live charts" />
      <Figure src={dark2} alt="Dark-theme market overview with watchlists" />
    </section>

    <section class="section stack">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Solution" title="Flexible and engaging.">
        <p>
          The solution gives users an easy way to interact with the platform. Three ideas shaped it: personalisation,
          interaction and a bit of fun.
        </p>
      </SectionHeader>
      <div class="stack stack--tight">
        <FeatureBox title="Dashboards that adapt to you">
          <p slot="text">
            Users can create and customise multiple dashboards, and choose which portfolio to show, at dashboard or
            widget level. It suits users who keep different portfolios for different reasons: one for regular checking,
            another for acting quickly on price changes.
          </p>
          <Figure src={dashboards} alt="Dashboard switcher with multiple custom dashboards" maxWidth={440} />
        </FeatureBox>
        <FeatureBox title="Drag and drop throughout">
          <p slot="text">
            Widgets can be arranged and rearranged on the dashboard, and market instruments can be added straight to a
            watchlist. Drag and drop works across the whole platform, which makes it feel quick and fun to use.
          </p>
          <Figure src={dragAndDrop} alt="Dragging an instrument onto a watchlist" maxWidth={440} />
        </FeatureBox>
        <FeatureBox title="Everything at a glance">
          <p slot="text">
            Real-time valuation of the portfolio sits next to live market data: prices, news and analyses. The
            instrument view brings performance and key information together in one place.
          </p>
          <Figure src={atAGlance} alt="Instrument view with performance chart and key figures" maxWidth={440} />
        </FeatureBox>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section stack">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Outcome & future steps" title="Delivered, and now on the go.">
        <p>
          We delivered the platform to VZ. Building on the responsive web version, we later developed a mobile version
          with reduced functionality, focused on use on the go.
        </p>
        <p>
          VZ presents its trading platform publicly with real-time prices, a customisable workspace and mobile access.
          The client’s feedback was good: users enjoyed the platform and found it easy to navigate, as beginners and as
          professionals. Additional features followed, such as maximising widgets that hold a lot of data and matter for
          decisions.
        </p>
        <p class="links">
          <a href="https://www.vermoegenszentrum.ch/en/investments/custody-accounts-at-vz" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >VZ trading platform <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={16} /></a
          >
          <a href="https://www.ti8m.com/en/products/digital-banking/trading-suite" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >ti&amp;m Trading <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={16} /></a
          >
        </p>
      </SectionHeader>
      <Figure src={mobile} alt="Trading Workbench mobile screens" />
    </section>
  </CaseStudy>

  <NextProject current="trading_workbench" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wireframes {
    gap: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
  }
  .wireframes :global(img) {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
</style>
